.TH INTRO 2 "January 2026" "TestUnix Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
intro \- introduction to system calls
.SH DESCRIPTION
Section 2 of the manual describes the system calls provided by the TestUnix kernel's native personality. These calls provide the interface between user-space applications and the kernel.
.PP
System calls are invoked via the `int 0x80` software interrupt. The system call number is passed in the EAX register, and arguments are passed in EBX, ECX, EDX, ESI, EDI, and EBP.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero or a positive value is returned. On failure, -1 is returned and the global variable `errno` is set to indicate the error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR personality (9),
.BR peso_native (9)
